music|organized-sound|NOUN|sounds arranged for expression or enjoyment|Sounds arranged through rhythm, melody, or other patterns for expression or enjoyment.|âm nhạc; nhạc|Soft music played while the guests found their seats.|Nhạc nhẹ vang lên trong lúc các vị khách tìm chỗ ngồi.|Usually uncountable; a piece of music names one work, rather than a music.|0
rupture|burst-open|VERB|tear or burst open|To tear or burst open, or cause something to do so.|vỡ; làm vỡ; rách|The frozen pipe ruptured during the night.|Đường ống bị đóng băng vỡ trong đêm.|Intransitive something ruptures or transitive rupture something; this example concerns a pipe, not medical advice.|-
september|calendar-month|NOUN|ninth month of the year|The month that follows August and comes before October.|tháng Chín|The new reading club begins in September.|Câu lạc bộ đọc sách mới bắt đầu vào tháng Chín.|Month name written September with a capital S; use in September, but on a particular September date.|0
whenever|every-time|CONJUNCTION|every time something happens|Each time that something happens.|mỗi khi|Whenever the door opens, a small bell rings.|Mỗi khi cửa mở, một chiếc chuông nhỏ reo lên.|Introduces a clause; the other clause describes what happens on each occasion.|0
whenever|any-time|CONJUNCTION|at any time that suits|At any time that a person chooses or that circumstances allow.|bất cứ khi nào|You can return the book whenever you finish reading it.|Bạn có thể trả sách bất cứ khi nào đọc xong.|Introduces a time clause; present finish can refer to a future occasion after can return.|0
clay|mouldable-earth|NOUN|fine earth that can be shaped when wet|Fine-grained earth that becomes easy to shape when mixed with water and is used for making pottery.|đất sét|The potter pressed the wet clay into a shallow dish.|Thợ gốm ép đất sét ướt thành một chiếc đĩa nông.|Uncountable for the material; a piece or lump of clay names an amount.|-
